***Array of pointers***
```c++
struct Student
{
	char name[10];
	int id;
	double gpa;
};

const int MAX_CLASS = 50;
Student class_array[MAX_CLASS];
Student * class_arrayP[MAX_CLASS]

class_arrayP[0] = new Student;
class_arrayP[1] = new Student; 
...

```

Uses less memory 

```c++
struct Student
{
	char name[10];
	int *id;
	double gpa;
};

Student joe;
joe.id = new int;
// MUST use new 
*(joe.id) = 112;
```
This is valid

```C++
Person {
	char name[10];
	int sin_num;
	Person spouse;
};
// This creates an issue
```

Instead,
```C++
Person {
	char name[10];
	int sin_num;
	Person* spouseP;
	// Careful, once you do this, spouseP is a NULL pointer.
};
```

